Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 03:38:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] R80b, part 6, patch 25 (cld-advisor, at main's word in M16;
 main's third folder, section 4, finding 7): B1030'S SCRIPT CARRIES THE
 CORRECTION OF THE ZERO BESIDE ITS OWN STATEMENT, AND THE ARC'S TEST HOLDS IT

A reader's supplement on the arcs main changed at Review 80 (agy-002's), its seventh finding, not checked by
main. Main's correction of 2026-11-11 (the freedom ledger's zero is not a computed quantity) stands on this
arc's page and in its verdict file. The arc's script says in a docstring that the ledger's verdict, a
retroactive freedom of 0.000, is untouched, with no mark; and the arc's own test held nothing of the
correction. (The lock of B1028 holds it on the page and in the verdict file.)

A dated note stands above the function whose docstring says it, in main's own words from the page. The
docstring is kept as it was written and what the function computes is not changed.

The arc's test gains one test under a dated note; none of main's is changed. It holds the correction in the
arc's three files, and in the script it holds it beside the statement: between the last blank line and the
statement. Planted: the script as it stood; the note moved to the head of the file; the correction taken
out of the page; main's sentence on B1028's verdict taken out of the verdict line; and a twin, a script
that no longer makes the statement.

MEASURED AND NOT MENDED: one more script under the arcs states the zero with no correction, the walk of
B1028 itself. It is the script that the correction is about, and whether it carries a note is main's.

The arc's test passes: 6 tests before, 7 with this one. Not checked by main. Tested against planted errors
by the session that wrote it.
---
 .../b1030_verify.py                           |  6 +++
 tests/test_b1030_price_lock.py                | 49 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 55 insertions(+)

diff --git a/frontier/B1030_price_lock_verification/b1030_verify.py b/frontier/B1030_price_lock_verification/b1030_verify.py
index 5b52e2ade..0facaab16 100644
--- a/frontier/B1030_price_lock_verification/b1030_verify.py
+++ b/frontier/B1030_price_lock_verification/b1030_verify.py
@@ -64,6 +64,12 @@ def v3_item1_defect():
     return {"in-place divisibility unfailable at length-weight 1": unfailable}
 
 
+# [NOTE 2026-11-12 (Review 80; a reader's supplement on the arcs main changed, its finding 7; not checked by main): the
+# docstring below says that the ledger's verdict, a retroactive freedom of 0.000, is untouched.  Main's correction of 2026-11-11
+# (the audit's finding E7), as it stands on this arc's page and in its verdict file: the freedom ledger's zero is not a
+# computed quantity. Its eleven links are each priced at zero by hand, and its check is that a phrase is found in the cited
+# arc's claim line.  B1028's verdict is OPEN.  The docstring is kept as it was written, and what the function computes is
+# not changed.]
 def v4_adoption_arithmetic():
     """The adoption, priced before anyone asks: with the trit adopted the discrete
     input bits become 3 + log2(3) = 4.585 -- EXACTLY B1028's conservative output
diff --git a/tests/test_b1030_price_lock.py b/tests/test_b1030_price_lock.py
index 01024e100..458a10ee8 100644
--- a/tests/test_b1030_price_lock.py
+++ b/tests/test_b1030_price_lock.py
@@ -73,3 +73,52 @@ def test_unit_obstruction_kappa_minus_two():
     assert sp.simplify(sp.Abs(kappa - 2) - 1) == 0
     assert sp.simplify(kappa - 2 - omega ** 2) == 0
     assert sp.simplify(sp.arg(kappa) + sp.pi / 6) == 0   # arg kappa = -pi/6 (the matter face)
+
+
+# 2026-11-12 (R80b, part 6; a reader's supplement on the arcs main changed at Review 80, its finding 7; not checked by main).
+# Main's correction of 2026-11-11 stands on this arc's page and in its verdict file, and the lock of B1028 holds it there.
+# The arc's script says the same thing in a docstring, with no mark; and this test file held nothing of the correction.
+# Nothing above this line is changed.
+THE_CORRECTION = "the freedom ledger's zero is not a computed quantity"
+WHAT_THE_SCRIPT_SAYS = "verdict (retroactive freedom 0.000) is untouched"
+
+
+def _where_the_correction_is_missing(page, verdict_file, script):
+    """the names of the three files of this arc in which the correction does not stand where the old statement does"""
+    bad = []
+    if THE_CORRECTION not in page:
+        bad.append("the page")
+    v = json.loads(verdict_file)
+    if THE_CORRECTION not in v["claim_one_line"] or "B1028's verdict is OPEN" not in v["claim_one_line"]:
+        bad.append("the verdict file")
+    flat = lambda s: " ".join(s.replace("#", " ").split())
+    if WHAT_THE_SCRIPT_SAYS in script:
+        head = script[:script.index(WHAT_THE_SCRIPT_SAYS)]
+        note = head[head.rindex("\n\n") if "\n\n" in head else 0:]             # what stands between the last blank line and the statement
+        if THE_CORRECTION not in flat(note) or "B1028's verdict is OPEN" not in flat(note):
+            bad.append("the script")
+    return bad
+
+
+def test_the_correction_of_the_zero_stands_in_the_arcs_three_files():
+    page = (ARC / "FINDINGS.md").read_text(encoding="utf-8")
+    verdict = (ARC / "arc_verdict.json").read_text(encoding="utf-8")
+    script = (ARC / "b1030_verify.py").read_text(encoding="utf-8")
+    assert script.count(WHAT_THE_SCRIPT_SAYS) == 1                              # the docstring is kept as it was written, and the note does not repeat it
+    assert _where_the_correction_is_missing(page, verdict, script) == []
+    # the script as it stood: the note taken out
+    i, j = script.index("# [NOTE 2026-11-12"), script.index("def v4_adoption_arithmetic():")
+    as_it_stood = script[:i] + script[j:]
+    assert WHAT_THE_SCRIPT_SAYS in as_it_stood and _where_the_correction_is_missing(page, verdict, as_it_stood) == ["the script"]
+    # the note moved to the head of the file, away from the statement, is not beside it
+    moved = script[i:j] + "\n\n" + as_it_stood
+    assert _where_the_correction_is_missing(page, verdict, moved) == ["the script"]
+    # the page and the verdict file with the correction taken out
+    assert _where_the_correction_is_missing(page.replace(THE_CORRECTION, ""), verdict, script) == ["the page"]
+    v = json.loads(verdict)
+    v["claim_one_line"] = v["claim_one_line"].replace("B1028's verdict is OPEN", "")
+    assert _where_the_correction_is_missing(page, json.dumps(v), script) == ["the verdict file"]
+    # the twin: a script that no longer makes the statement needs no note
+    assert _where_the_correction_is_missing(page, verdict, as_it_stood.replace(WHAT_THE_SCRIPT_SAYS, "")) == []
+    # what the function computes is what it computed
+    assert all(_cells().v4_adoption_arithmetic().values())
